Translate Persian that sits beside a value in JSX (1.15.1)

The first sweep matched `>text<`, which misses the shape

    {project.doneTaskCount}/{project.totalTaskCount} تسک
    ددلاین {task.dueDate}

where the words sit next to an expression rather than between two tags.
That is where every remaining report came from. A second sweep found 22
of them across 46 files; the rest of its hits were JSX comments.

Each became a parameterised key — tr('{done}/{total} tasks', …) — which
also lets a translator put the number where their language wants it,
rather than assuming it comes first.

The dialog subtitles for adding a member and a client were plain literals
too, and `editLabel`, `placeholder` and `emptyText` are now recognised by
the extractor alongside `header` and `addLabel`.

Checked the reported duplicate statuses on the server: the database holds
exactly 32 tags with no duplicates, so nothing to fix there.

